      </events>\n        <status>available</status>\n      </show>\n      <show id=\"1173692423\">\n        <name>\n          <![CDATA[SCHOOL OF ROCK (Relaxed Screening)]]>\n        </name>\n        <description>\n          <![CDATA[<div>\n<font size=\"5\"><b>School of Rock&nbsp;</b></font><img src=\"https://d1bry8u3byci8.cloudfront.net/as-assets/variants/x1mrfg5u7s7k0mwf627cgikpu1zf/a6206d8b8848d1f5f779dd436f25589e3a792fee204effd13dccee565e881abd\" style=\"font-size:0.875rem;\">\n</div><div><font size=\"3\">Genre(s): Comedy/Music</font></div><div><font size=\"3\">GER/USA | 2003 | 109 mins</font></div><div><font size=\"3\">Director: Richard Linklater</font></div><div><font size=\"3\">Stars:&nbsp;Jack Black, Joan Cusack, Adam Pascal, Lucas Papaelias</font></div><div><p><font size=\"3\">Having been sacked by his band No\nVacancy, Dewey Finn (Black) lands a temporary post as teacher at a local\nprimary school. After overhearing his class in a music lesson, he hatches an\naudacious plan to form a rock band from the best pupils, enter them in the\nlocal Battle of the Bands competition and so embarrass his ex-band, who are\nalso entering. Jack Black has his own rock band, as well as being a consummate\ncomedian, and ensures you will be rocking (and rolling) with laughter.</font></p></div>]]>\n        </description>\n        <event_category>Relaxed Screening</event_category>\n        <production_company_name></production_company_name>\n        <priority>0</priority>\n        <url>https://www.davidleancinema.uk/#whatson</url>\n        <version>53</version>\n        <tags>\n        </tags>\n        <images>\n          <image priority=\"90\">\n            <url size=\"large\">https://d1bry8u3byci8.cloudfront.net/as-assets/variants/awyv6fkdfs9g3t3fuhgbdibx3rsy/a6206d8b8848d1f5f779dd436f25589e3a792fee204effd13dccee565e881abd</url>\n            <url size=\"medium\">https://d1bry8u3byci8.cloudfront.net/as-assets/variants/awyv6fkdfs9g3t3fuhgbdibx3rsy/6428308680a2820b32ca9af5ca523d2